The Reaper is the neutral elite of the Sweeper (Halberdier route; no alignment
asked). Its glaive reaps a whole battlefield: a Sweep strikes the row behind
its target too, and the Sweep itself comes back every other round at the top
rank.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Reaping sweep  Sweep also strikes the foes in the row behind its target,
                    each at 50% of a blow's damage
  35 Long glaive    +3 Attack
  40 Wider arc      the row behind takes 75% of a blow's damage from a Sweep
  45 Reaper's toll  +1 damage on every blow
  50 Hardened       +10% maximum health
  55 Reaper's eye   +5% critical chance
  60 Harvest        Sweep is ready two rounds sooner than a Sweeper's: every
                    other round is a Sweep

It needs the Sweeper first (<ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] reaper confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Halberdier talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Iron Hide (+5 Armor), Veteran's
Edge (+3 Attack), Second Wind (once a battle, below a quarter of its health at
the start of its turn, heals a tenth of its maximum). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
